  m_Name: Triceratops
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Triceratops
  description: Triceratops was a huge herbivorous ceratopsid dinosaur from the late
    Cretaceous. Its name means three horned face which it gets from having three
    horns on its head. They were mainly found in North America. As adults, they grew
    up to 9 m (30 ft) long by 3 m (9.8 ft) tall and probably weighed around 12 t
    (26,000 lb). Fully-grown, their skull was enormous (two meters long and nearly
    a meter wide).
